      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Sales quoting - average, would only respond to questions with pro forma quotes.  No phone calls and did not answer questions asked via email.The installers were really nice people.  Just sparkies sent out to do a job.  They were polite, they were tidy.  Most of the work was to a very good quality but a few things could have been better. External Cat 6 cable unprotected and cable tied to external conduit, solid conduit bent over existing conduit rather than using flexible conduit, additions to fuse box not straight.Customer service was very average. They send you a txt telling you to call them to confirm your install date. The inverter was lost in transit, we we advised by the installers on the day of install but no communication from the office.  When we finally received a txt (not even a phone call) regarding the rescheduled appointment to install inverter they lied about the cause of the problem stating it was due to a sick staff member.  They were unaware that the installers had already told us the truth that the inverter was lost in transit. Then somehow the customer service lady was suggesting she was doing use a favour when rescheduling as if we should be grateful.",
